<http://data.silknow.org/object/4c5796be-c320-3d60-97d4-3125d7d8723f>
        a                       ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment            "Middle East, Textile; Dress fabric of silk and metal thread, Iran, 1800-1870"@en , "Dress fabric of silk and metal thread.\n\nWoven silk and metal thread, plain weave ground.\nThere are seven pieces joined together, four of which are described as [a] and three of which are described as [b].\n[a] metal thread ground with a small ogival lattice in white decorated with small red and green leaves.  In the centre of each compartment is a flower spray with green stems and leaves and red flowers.\nWarp: pink silk,\nWeft: white, pink and green silk.\nMetal thread: silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk.\n[b] Very similar to the pattern described above but the central flower of each spray is edged with more white and has details in blue.\nWarp: pink silk,\nWeft: white, pink, blue and green silk, metal thread: silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk."@en ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note        "Middle East, Textile; Dress fabric of silk and metal thread, Iran, 1800-1870"@en , "Dress fabric of silk and metal thread.\n\nWoven silk and metal thread, plain weave ground.\nThere are seven pieces joined together, four of which are described as [a] and three of which are described as [b].\n[a] metal thread ground with a small ogival lattice in white decorated with small red and green leaves.  In the centre of each compartment is a flower spray with green stems and leaves and red flowers.\nWarp: pink silk,\nWeft: white, pink and green silk.\nMetal thread: silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk.\n[b] Very similar to the pattern described above but the central flower of each spray is edged with more white and has details in blue.\nWarp: pink silk,\nWeft: white, pink, blue and green silk, metal thread: silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk."@en ;
